WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
The ocean holds about 50 times
as much carbon as the atmosphere.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:11.730
And between 2015 and 2024, it took up
29 per cent of all the CO₂ we emitted.

3
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.530
That is carbon the atmosphere never kept.

4
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.230
So isn't the ocean doing us a favour?

5
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.310
Not for coral reefs.

6
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.970
Why is the ocean's uptake
of CO₂ bad news for them?

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.410
In this mission, you'll follow carbon
into the deep ocean through the solubility

8
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.810
pump and the biological pump.

9
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.770
Then you'll read the latest
Great Barrier Reef data,

10
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.710
region by region, and weigh
what is driving its losses.

11
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.910
Your mission: explain why the ocean's
uptake of CO₂ is bad news for coral

12
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:42.610
reefs.
